      "seq": 140,
      "game_seq": 298,
      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "Opponent's at 10 life with Iguana Parrot, Deserters, and a counter-laden Wan Shi Tong on board. Since Wan Shi Tong has counters, Heartless Act can't destroy it outright, but the proliferate-removal mode could strip counters down to shrink it to 1/1.\n\
\n\
My attackers total exactly 10 damage across Warden, two Archers, and Colony, but with three blockers they'll trade down and survive around 6 life if I just swing wide. A better line: play my sixth land, use Heartless Act to knock Wan Shi Tong to 1/1, then attack — combined with Warden's activated ability pinging for extra damage, I might have enough reach to close things out this turn instead of next.\n\
\n\
Actually the cleanest line seems to be Swamp into Heartless Act on Wan Shi Tong, then swing wide — my X/1 attackers trade down against their blockers, but I still push through Warden plus some extra damage, putting them into the 5-7 range. I'm weighing whether holding back Archers to avoid a bad trade is better than committing the full attack.\n\
\n\
Also considering Act mode 1 on Parrot instead — killing it outright — but shrinking Wan Shi Tong to a 1/1 neuters their biggest threat more effectively, so I'll go with mode 2 on WST.\n\
\n\
Then attack with everything, and use Warden's ability once more since I'll have enough mana left after casting Act.\n\
\n\
