      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "I already missed casting Heartless Act precombat, but I can still cast it as an instant during combat — if WST blocks, I could strip its counters down to make it a 1/1 and let it die in combat instead.\n\
\n\
Opponent sits at 10 life with three possible blockers (WST flying vigilance, Parrot flying, Deserters) against my four attackers totaling 10 damage plus a possible 1 from Warden's ping, and their lands are tapped so no tricks are coming. I'm working through how they'd likely assign blocks across Warden (menace), both Archers, and flying Colony to minimize damage taken, checking which trades favor them.\n\
\n\
Since I'm at 16 and their crackback with WST/Parrot isn't threatening, attacking with everything is clearly correct — worst case I trade some creatures but come out ahead given I'm holding removal to clean up blockers if needed.\n\
\n\
