      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "I'm already in combat and realize I never cast Heartless Act mode 2 precombat — Wan Shi Tong still has its 3 counters, sitting at 4/4 instead of base 1/1. Now I'm weighing whether I can still use it effectively this late, since removing counters mid-combat changes the calculus versus casting it in the main phase.\n\
\n\
Killing Deserters precombat with Heartless Act seems stronger than post-block removal, since blocked damage still won't get through either way. If I clear Deserters first, they're left with only WST and Parrot to block, letting Warden and Colony punch through for 4-6 damage depending on their block choices, plus the ping ability. Post-block, shrinking WST to trade with a blocked Archers is also decent value, but doesn't push extra damage through.\n\
\n\
With 6 lands, I can Heartless Act plus ping with Warden and still have mana up, using firebending during combat if needed. My biggest risk is my fragile 3/1 Archers dying to almost any blocker, while Colony trades evenly with Parrot — so the safest line is likely killing Deserters before combat to maximize unblocked damage.\n\
\n\
Even if their WST swings back at 16 flying, I'll be fine taking that hit. They're at 10 and forced into heavy blocks, so attacking with everything is the right call.\n\
\n\
