      "thinking": "I'm calculating mana: playing the Swamp gives 8 lands, and attacking with Warden triggers firebending for an extra red mana, bringing me to 9 total—enough for three pings during combat to bring the opponent down to 3 life, while checking if Parrot and Yue can still block.\n\
\n\
If they let Warden through unblocked, 2 combat damage plus three pings would actually be lethal at 5, so they're forced to double-block and kill Warden, netting me only three pings and leaving me creatureless afterward. Weighing that against just pinging twice without attacking and holding Warden back as a blocker, since next turn their Yue, Parrot, and Unagi attack for 10 total and I need Warden to at least chump or trade with something to survive.\n\
\n\
Actually, this turn I only have 6 mana available for pings, dropping opponent to 3. Next turn, untapping 8 lands plus attacking with Warden for the extra R gives me 9 mana, enough for three pings — exactly lethal from 3, provided Warden survives their attack. If they swing with Unagi and I take it unblocked, I'm at 1 life, but as long as they lack removal or bounce for Warden, I win on my following turn.\n\
\n\
That Unagi trigger isn't relevant here. So I'll just play the Swamp and ping twice this turn.\n\
\n\
