      "thinking": "The turn labeling seems off, but I'm at 11 with the opponent at 3, facing 10 incoming damage from Yue, Parrot, and Unagi combined. If I don't block, I drop to 1; blocking Unagi with Warden trades my Warden for a reduction to 6 life instead.\n\
\n\
Blocking Parrot instead lets Warden survive (2 damage against 3 toughness) while killing Parrot, dropping me to 3. Next turn I'd have 8 lands plus an attack trigger giving me 9 mana for three pings—exactly lethal against their 3 life, assuming Warden survives combat and nothing disrupts the plan like a bounce or counter. Since my turn comes before theirs, blocking Parrot to preserve Warden and go to 3 life looks like the safer route to winning on my next turn.\n\
\n\
losing my board too. Life total barely matters here since I'm either winning soon or dying to their fliers regardless, so I'll skip the block and keep Warden safe.\n\
\n\
