      "reasoning": null,
      "thinking": "Opponent's at 3 life with 4 untapped lands against my 8. I could attack with Warden for the extra mana then ping three times for lethal, or ping twice first then attack to generate the final ping's mana - either way it requires connecting with Warden, and the risk is they hold up removal for it.\n\
\n\
If they kill Warden in response to a ping activation, the ability still resolves independently since it's already on the stack, but I lose access to any further activations. Comparing sequencing: pinging twice precombat then attacking leaves me needing that last activation post-combat, while attacking first and using the combat mana for all three pings front-loads the risk to just the first activation - either way a single removal spell costs me exactly one ping's worth of damage.\n\
\n\
I should just attack and try to stack the pings during the declare attackers step once the trigger resolves.\n\
\n\
